{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What is the objective of this packing plan — are we minimizing the number of containers used, maximizing the total weight (or total units) of goods shipped, or something else?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the optimization objective, presenting mutually exclusive options for one decision."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are we required to ship all available goods (i.e., use up all 120 A, 90 B, 300 C, 90 D, 120 E), or are the available quantities just upper limits and it's acceptable to leave some goods unshipped?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for a policy choice regarding whether inventory must be fully utilized or if it serves as an upper limit."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there a fixed number of containers available to choose from (i.e., an upper bound on how many containers we can use), or can we use as many containers as needed as long as each used one satisfies the 18–60 ton and 12-unit-D rules?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the upper bound on the number of containers, presenting two mutually exclusive options."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are the goods units indivisible (each unit must be loaded whole, so container loads are integer numbers of units), or can units be split fractionally?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the divisibility of goods units."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The rule \"if a container contains any type A then it must also contain at least one type C\" — does this apply per container (i.e., each individual container that has A must have at least 1 C in that same container), or is it a global rule across all containers?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the scope of a specific rule (per-container vs. global)."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since we're minimizing the number of containers and it's acceptable to leave goods unshipped, is there any requirement that at least one container must be used (i.e., we must ship at least some goods), or is it acceptable for the optimal solution to use zero containers and ship nothing?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether the solution must use at least one container or if zero containers are allowed."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there any other business rule or constraint I should be aware of that isn't already stated — for example, a maximum number of units of a single type per container, a requirement that each container must contain at least one unit of every type, or a rule about which types can or cannot be mixed in the same container?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single open-ended question about the existence of other unstated business rules or constraints. The examples provided are illustrative of the type of information requested, not separate independent questions."
}
